  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "Humans and gorillas are mapped as analogous beings who love to relax",
  "description": "The text 'after 3 million years of evolution we still love to relax' creates an analogical mapping between the human man (visual entity) and the gorilla (visual entity). The text implies that despite vast evolutionary differences, both species share a fundamental, unchanged behavior of relaxation. The visual juxtaposition of both entities in similar relaxed poses reinforces this mapping. This mapping is central to the meme's humor and its underlying harmful stereotype, as it equates human leisure with primate behavior, implicitly referencing the anti-Black stereotype of comparing Black people to primates.",
